25,gemma3:12b,0.2,CWE-094,True,CWE-94,"The `genDefaultResourceYaml` method constructs a YAML string using user-provided input (`k8sNamespace.getNamespace()`, `k8sNamespace.getLimitsCpu()`, and `k8sNamespace.getLimitsMemory()`). This allows an attacker to inject malicious commands or data into the YAML, which could be executed when the generated YAML is used by Kubernetes. Specifically, if a user provides a namespace name containing shell metacharacters (e.g., `;`), these characters will be interpreted as commands when `resourceYaml` is replaced with them.",2839.08
