44,gemma3:12b,0.5,CWE-094,True,CWE-20,"The `streamToString` method reads the entire input stream into a byte array before converting it to a string. If the YAML file is excessively large, this could lead to a denial of service (DoS) by exhausting available memory.",1635.01
45,gemma3:12b,0.0,CWE-094,True,CWE-20,"The `streamToString` method reads the entire input stream into a byte array before converting it to a string. If the YAML file is very large, this could lead to an out-of-memory error (Denial of Service).  While unlikely in typical usage scenarios, a malicious actor could craft extremely large YAML files to exhaust server resources.",2000.97
