45,gemma3:12b,0.5,CWE-094,True,CWE-20,"The `streamToString` method reads the entire input stream into a byte array using `stream.read(bytes)`. The size of the byte array is determined by `stream.available()`, which represents the number of bytes immediately available in the stream without blocking. If the YAML file is excessively large, this could lead to an out-of-memory error (OOM), effectively a denial-of-service vulnerability.  An attacker could potentially craft a very large YAML file to exhaust server resources.",2569.41
