60,gemma3:12b,0.0,CWE-079,True,CWE-79,"The code constructs the `title` attribute of an anchor tag using user-supplied input (`m_title`). If this input is not properly sanitized, it could lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities. An attacker could inject malicious JavaScript into the `title` attribute, which would then be executed in the victim's browser when they hover over the link.",2287.02
60,gemma3:12b,0.2,CWE-079,True,CWE-79,"The code constructs the `title` attribute of an anchor tag using user-supplied input (`m_title`). If this input is not properly sanitized, it could lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities. An attacker could inject malicious JavaScript into the `title` attribute, which would then be executed in the victim's browser when they hover over the link.",1997.94
60,gemma3:12b,0.5,CWE-079,True,CWE-79,"The `setTitle` method allows user-controlled input (`m_title`) to be directly embedded into the HTML output via the `title` attribute of an anchor tag. If this value is not properly sanitized or encoded, it could lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities. An attacker can inject malicious JavaScript code into the `title` attribute, which will then be executed in the victim's browser when they hover over the link.",2327.51
61,gemma3:12b,0.0,CWE-079,True,CWE-79,"The code constructs an HTML anchor tag using user-supplied input (`m_title` and `m_accesskey`) without proper sanitization. This makes the application vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks. An attacker could inject malicious JavaScript into these attributes, which would then be executed in the victim's browser when they view the page.",1944.8
61,gemma3:12b,0.2,CWE-079,True,CWE-79,"The code constructs an HTML anchor tag using user-supplied input (`m_title` and `m_accesskey`) without proper sanitization. This makes the application vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks. An attacker could inject malicious JavaScript by setting these attributes, which would then be executed in the victim's browser.",1908.19
61,gemma3:12b,0.5,CWE-079,True,CWE-79,"The code constructs the `title` attribute of the anchor tag using user-supplied input (`m_title`). This is vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) if the value of `m_title` comes from an untrusted source (e.g., a request parameter or database). An attacker could inject malicious JavaScript code into the `m_title` attribute, which would then be executed in the user's browser when they hover over the link.",2253.01
62,gemma3:12b,0.0,CWE-079,True,CWE-79,"The code constructs an HTML anchor tag using user-supplied input (`m_title` and `m_accesskey`) without proper sanitization. This makes the application vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks. An attacker could inject malicious JavaScript into these attributes, which would then be executed in the victim's browser when they view the page.",1938.48
