142,gemma3:12b,0.0,CWE-022,True,CWE-915,"The `globToRegex` method is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). The function converts glob patterns into regular expressions. A maliciously crafted glob pattern can be converted into a regex that takes an extremely long time to match, potentially causing the server to hang or become unresponsive. Specifically, nested quantifiers and complex character classes within the glob pattern can lead to exponential backtracking in the regex engine.",3479.05
142,gemma3:12b,0.2,CWE-022,True,CWE-915,"The `globToRegex` method is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). The nested group handling logic involving '{' and '}' characters can lead to exponential backtracking if the input pattern contains maliciously crafted sequences. This can cause excessive CPU consumption, potentially leading to a denial-of-service condition.",2020.28
142,gemma3:12b,0.5,CWE-022,True,CWE-20,"The `globToRegex` method is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). The function converts glob patterns into regular expressions. A malicious user could craft a specially designed glob pattern that, when converted to a regex, would cause the regex engine to take an extremely long time to match against any input string, leading to a denial-of-service condition. Specifically, nested quantifiers or complex character classes can be used to create such patterns.",2437.66
143,gemma3:12b,0.0,CWE-022,True,CWE-915,"The `globToRegex` method is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). The function converts glob patterns into regular expressions. A maliciously crafted glob pattern can be converted into a regex that takes an extremely long time to match, potentially causing the server to hang or become unresponsive. Specifically, nested quantifiers and complex character classes within the glob pattern can lead to exponential backtracking in the regex engine.",2283.66
143,gemma3:12b,0.2,CWE-022,True,CWE-915,"The `globToRegex` method is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). The function converts glob patterns into regular expressions. A maliciously crafted glob pattern can lead to an exponential backtracking situation in the resulting regex, causing excessive CPU usage and potentially crashing the server. Specifically, nested quantifiers or complex alternations within a malicious glob could trigger this.",2151.37
143,gemma3:12b,0.5,CWE-022,True,CWE-915,"The `globToRegex` method is vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS). The nested logic and character handling within the function can lead to exponential backtracking when processing malicious glob patterns. A carefully crafted glob pattern could cause the regex engine to consume excessive resources, potentially leading to a denial-of-service condition.",2042.32
