207,gemma3:12b,0.2,CWE-078,True,CWE-20,"The code uses `shellRunner.runShell()` to execute shell commands for user and group management. This introduces a command injection vulnerability if the input parameters (e.g., usernames, group names) are not properly sanitized before being passed to the shell commands. An attacker could potentially inject malicious commands into these parameters, leading to arbitrary code execution on the server.",2195.23
207,gemma3:12b,0.5,CWE-078,True,CWE-20,"The code uses `shellRunner.runShell()` to execute shell commands for user and group management. This introduces a command injection vulnerability if the properties `EXCLUDE_USER_PROPERTY` or `EXCLUDE_GROUP_PROPERTY` are controlled by an attacker. The values of these properties are used to construct regex patterns, but there's no sanitization performed before constructing the pattern. An attacker can inject arbitrary shell commands into these properties which will be executed with the privileges of the process running this code.",2662.78
208,gemma3:12b,0.0,CWE-078,True,CWE-20,"The code uses `shellRunner.runShell()` to execute shell commands for user and group management. This introduces a command injection vulnerability if the shell commands are constructed using unsanitized input from external sources (e.g., configuration properties or environment variables). An attacker could potentially inject arbitrary commands into these shell calls, leading to unauthorized access or system compromise.",2220.48
208,gemma3:12b,0.2,CWE-078,True,CWE-20,"The code uses `shellRunner.runShell()` to execute shell commands for user and group management. This introduces a command injection vulnerability if the shell commands are constructed using unsanitized input from external sources (e.g., configuration properties or environment variables). An attacker could potentially inject arbitrary commands into these shell calls, leading to unauthorized access or system compromise.",2228.4
208,gemma3:12b,0.5,CWE-078,True,CWE-20,"The code uses `shellRunner.runShell()` to execute shell commands for user and group management. This is vulnerable to command injection if the shell commands are constructed using unsanitized input from external sources (e.g., configuration properties, environment variables). The code retrieves these values via `AuthorizerConfigurationContext` which could be influenced by an attacker. Although the code attempts to validate some inputs with regex patterns (`excludeUsers`, `excludeGroups`), it doesn't sanitize or validate all shell command parameters, leaving room for malicious commands to be injected and executed on the system.",2905.93
