813,gemma3:12b,0.2,CWE-079,True,CWE-78,"The code uses NekoHTML to parse HTML input. While it attempts to sanitize the input by stripping invalid XML characters, this is not sufficient to prevent all types of injection attacks. Specifically, conditional directives (e.g., `<?php echo ... ?>`) can be injected into the HTML and executed if they are not properly handled or escaped before parsing. The regex used to strip these directives (`conditionalDirectives`) might be bypassed with clever encoding or obfuscation techniques.",2594.76
